# WHSLocDirAction Batch Copy Extension

## Quick Overview

This D365 Finance & Operations extension solves the problem of losing custom query configurations when converting Location Directive Actions to batch-enabled versions.

### The Problem

In D365FO, Location Directive Actions have a "Batch enabled" field. When you toggle this field from **No** to **Yes**, the system automatically resets the underlying query, causing you to lose:
- Custom table joins
- Filter ranges
- Sort orders
- All other query customizations

### The Solution

This extension provides:

1. **Copy to Batch Button** - One-click copy of an action to a batch-enabled version while preserving the query
2. **Mass Function** - Bulk processing to convert multiple actions across multiple location directives
3. **Idempotent Processing** - Safe to run multiple times without creating duplicates

---

## Features

### ✅ Query Preservation

All query customizations are preserved:
- Standard and custom ranges
- Inner joins, outer joins, exists joins
- Multi-table joins
- Sort orders
- Field selections
- Complex filter expressions

### ✅ One-Click Copy

- Button on Location Directive form (Actions grid)
- Enabled only when action is not batch-enabled
- Creates new action with unique sequence number
- Marks source action as "Copied" to prevent duplicates

### ✅ Mass Processing

- Dialog-based selection of location directives
- Filter by warehouse, work type, directive code, etc.
- Processes all eligible actions in selected directives
- Progress reporting via info log
- Skips already-processed records

### ✅ Safety Features

- Transaction integrity (ttsbegin/ttscommit)
- Error handling and rollback
- Idempotent execution (no duplicates)
- Audit trail (Copied flag)

